@jamorham Do I understand correctly that the "Samsung Workaround" setting should be always set for all devices?
And, there is an intelligence in the code that only kicks in, to enable Buggy Samsung Workaround, if the device needs the workaround?

But, what happens if the wake up jitter is detected and the Buggy Samsung Workaround is enabled for a non-Samsung device?  Could that never happen?
